{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "sentences-around",
  "title": "Getting Around",
  "description": "Sentences for getting from place to place and running errands: asking the way, taking transport, ordering food, shopping, and sorting out your room.",
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "s-17",
      "indonesian": "Saya mau ke pasar.",
      "english": "I'm going to the market.",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "t": "Saya ",
          "w": "w-saya"
        },
        {
          "t": "mau ",
          "w": "w-mau"
        },
        {
          "t": "ke pasar.",
          "w": "w-pasar"
        }
      ],
      "pitfallNote": "No verb for 'go' is needed: mau ke is 'going to (a place)'. Ke is 'to', and di is 'at'.",
      "audio": "audio/id/sentences/s-17.mp3",
      "tags": [
        "errands",
        "places"
      ],
      "difficulty": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "s-18",
      "indonesian": "Stasiunnya jauh dari sini?",
      "english": "Is the station far from here?",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "t": "Stasiunnya ",
          "w": "w-stasiun"
        },
        {
          "t": "jauh ",
          "w": "w-jauh"
        },
        {
          "t": "dari sini?",
          "w": "w-dari"
        }
      ],
      "registerNotes": "A rising voice is all it takes to make a question. The -nya on stasiun works like 'the': the station you both have in mind.",
      "audio": "audio/id/sentences/s-18.mp3",
      "tags": [
        "directions",
        "questions"
      ],
      "difficulty": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "s-19",
      "indonesian": "Permisi, saya cari apotek.",
      "english": "Excuse me, I'm looking for a pharmacy.",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "t": "Permisi, "
        },
        {
          "t": "saya ",
          "w": "w-saya"
        },
        {
          "t": "cari ",
          "w": "w-cari"
        },
        {
          "t": "apotek.",
          "w": "w-apotek"
        }
      ],
      "registerNotes": "Saying what you're looking for is the simplest way to ask the way. Permisi first catches someone's attention politely.",
      "audio": "audio/id/sentences/s-19.mp3",
      "tags": [
        "directions",
        "errands"
      ],
      "difficulty": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "s-20",
      "indonesian": "Berapa lama ke bandara?",
      "english": "How long does it take to get to the airport?",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "t": "Berapa ",
          "w": "w-berapa"
        },
        {
          "t": "lama ",
          "w": "w-lama"
        },
        {
          "t": "ke bandara?",
          "w": "w-bandara"
        }
      ],
      "registerNotes": "Berapa lama asks how long. Add dari sini (from here) if it isn't clear where you're starting from.",
      "audio": "audio/id/sentences/s-20.mp3",
      "tags": [
        "transport",
        "time"
      ],
      "difficulty": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "s-21",
      "indonesian": "Dari sini ke stasiun naik apa?",
      "english": "How do I get to the station from here?",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "t": "Dari sini ",
          "w": "w-dari"
        },
        {
          "t": "ke stasiun ",
          "w": "w-stasiun"
        },
        {
          "t": "naik apa?",
          "w": "w-apa"
        }
      ],
      "registerNotes": "Naik apa? (ride what?) asks which transport to take. The answer might be naik bus, naik ojek or jalan kaki (walk).",
      "audio": "audio/id/sentences/s-21.mp3",
      "tags": [
        "transport",
        "directions"
      ],
      "difficulty": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "s-22",
      "indonesian": "Haltenya di seberang jalan.",
      "english": "The bus stop is across the road.",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "t": "Haltenya ",
          "w": "w-halte"
        },
        {
          "t": "di seberang ",
          "w": "w-di"
        },
        {
          "t": "jalan.",
          "w": "w-jalan"
        }
      ],
      "registerNotes": "Di seberang is 'on the other side of': di seberang jalan, across the road; di seberang sungai, across the river.",
      "audio": "audio/id/sentences/s-22.mp3",
      "tags": [
        "directions",
        "transport"
      ],
      "difficulty": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "s-23",
      "indonesian": "Rumah sakitnya di depan masjid.",
      "english": "The hospital's opposite the mosque.",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "t": "Rumah sakitnya ",
          "w": "w-rumah-sakit"
        },
        {
          "t": "di depan ",
          "w": "w-depan"
        },
        {
          "t": "masjid.",
          "w": "w-masjid"
        }
      ],
      "registerNotes": "Di depan is 'in front of', and across a road it means 'opposite'. Mosques make good landmarks: most neighbourhoods have one.",
      "audio": "audio/id/sentences/s-23.mp3",
      "tags": [
        "directions",
        "places"
      ],
      "difficulty": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "s-24",
      "indonesian": "Pantainya tidak jauh dari hotel kami.",
      "english": "The beach isn't far from our hotel.",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "t": "Pantainya ",
          "w": "w-pantai"
        },
        {
          "t": "tidak jauh ",
          "w": "w-jauh"
        },
        {
          "t": "dari hotel ",
          "w": "w-hotel"
        },
        {
          "t": "kami.",
          "w": "w-kami"
        }
      ],
      "pitfallNote": "Kami, not kita: the person you're telling isn't staying at your hotel.",
      "audio": "audio/id/sentences/s-24.mp3",
      "tags": [
        "places",
        "travel"
      ],
      "difficulty": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "s-25",
      "indonesian": "Tolong berhenti di depan hotel itu.",
      "english": "Please stop in front of that hotel.",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "t": "Tolong "
        },
        {
          "t": "berhenti ",
          "w": "w-berhenti"
        },
        {
          "t": "di depan ",
          "w": "w-depan"
        },
        {
          "t": "hotel ",
          "w": "w-hotel"
        },
        {
          "t": "itu.",
          "w": "w-itu"
        }
      ],
      "registerNotes": "Tolong turns an instruction into a request. To a driver, add Pak or Mas at the end: … hotel itu, Pak.",
      "audio": "audio/id/sentences/s-25.mp3",
      "tags": [
        "transport",
        "requests"
      ],
      "difficulty": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "s-26",
      "indonesian": "Besok kami ke Yogyakarta naik kereta.",
      "english": "Tomorrow we're going to Yogyakarta by train.",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "t": "Besok ",
          "w": "w-besok"
        },
        {
          "t": "kami ",
          "w": "w-kami"
        },
        {
          "t": "ke Yogyakarta ",
          "w": "w-ke"
        },
        {
          "t": "naik kereta."
        }
      ],
      "registerNotes": "Naik (get on, ride) is how you say 'by': naik kereta, by train; naik bus, by bus; naik pesawat, by plane.",
      "audio": "audio/id/sentences/s-26.mp3",
      "tags": [
        "travel",
        "transport"
      ],
      "difficulty": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "s-27",
      "indonesian": "Jalannya macet karena banjir.",
      "english": "The roads are jammed because of the flooding.",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "t": "Jalannya ",
          "w": "w-jalan"
        },
        {
          "t": "macet "
        },
        {
          "t": "karena ",
          "w": "w-karena"
        },
        {
          "t": "banjir.",
          "w": "w-banjir"
        }
      ],
      "registerNotes": "Macet, traffic that's barely moving, is a word you'll hear every day in Jakarta. Karena before a noun means 'because of'.",
      "audio": "audio/id/sentences/s-27.mp3",
      "tags": [
        "transport",
        "weather"
      ],
      "difficulty": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "s-28",
      "indonesian": "Toko itu tutup hari Minggu.",
      "english": "That shop is closed on Sundays.",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "t": "Toko ",
          "w": "w-toko"
        },
        {
          "t": "itu ",
          "w": "w-itu"
        },
        {
          "t": "tutup "
        },
        {
          "t": "hari Minggu.",
          "w": "w-hari-minggu"
        }
      ],
      "pitfallNote": "No word for 'on' before a day, and no plural: hari Minggu covers 'on Sundays'.",
      "audio": "audio/id/sentences/s-28.mp3",
      "tags": [
        "shopping",
        "time"
      ],
      "difficulty": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "s-29",
      "indonesian": "Warung ini buka sampai jam berapa?",
      "english": "How late is this warung open?",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "t": "Warung ",
          "w": "w-warung"
        },
        {
          "t": "ini ",
          "w": "w-ini"
        },
        {
          "t": "buka "
        },
        {
          "t": "sampai ",
          "w": "w-sampai"
        },
        {
          "t": "jam berapa?",
          "w": "w-jam"
        }
      ],
      "registerNotes": "Buka is 'open' and tutup 'closed'. Sampai jam berapa? asks 'until what time?'",
      "audio": "audio/id/sentences/s-29.mp3",
      "tags": [
        "food",
        "time"
      ],
      "difficulty": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "s-30",
      "indonesian": "Saya harus ke bank sebelum jam tiga.",
      "english": "I have to get to the bank before three.",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "t": "Saya ",
          "w": "w-saya"
        },
        {
          "t": "harus ",
          "w": "w-harus"
        },
        {
          "t": "ke bank ",
          "w": "w-bank"
        },
        {
          "t": "sebelum "
        },
        {
          "t": "jam tiga.",
          "w": "w-jam"
        }
      ],
      "registerNotes": "Harus (must, have to) goes before the verb, or straight before ke when the going is understood.",
      "audio": "audio/id/sentences/s-30.mp3",
      "tags": [
        "errands",
        "time"
      ],
      "difficulty": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "s-31",
      "indonesian": "Saya mau mi goreng, tapi jangan terlalu pedas.",
      "english": "I'd like fried noodles, but not too spicy.",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "t": "Saya ",
          "w": "w-saya"
        },
        {
          "t": "mau ",
          "w": "w-mau"
        },
        {
          "t": "mi goreng, ",
          "w": "w-mi"
        },
        {
          "t": "tapi ",
          "w": "w-tapi"
        },
        {
          "t": "jangan terlalu "
        },
        {
          "t": "pedas.",
          "w": "w-pedas"
        }
      ],
      "registerNotes": "Jangan terlalu pedas is 'not too spicy'. If you can't take any chilli at all, ask for it tidak pedas sama sekali.",
      "audio": "audio/id/sentences/s-31.mp3",
      "tags": [
        "food",
        "ordering"
      ],
      "difficulty": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "s-32",
      "indonesian": "Teh panas, tidak pakai gula, ya.",
